WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.130
- I got my merch on.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.470
Do you have your merch on?

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.480
We're about to watch the Rocky movies,

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.130
talk about some of the health effects

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.790
that my man Rocco has faced.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:08.870
Let's get into it.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:09.890
Be woo!

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:10.963
Hey, yo, Rocco.

00:00:13.432 --> 00:00:17.180
I never understood why boxers
did this back in the day,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.810
or frankly, any athletes.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.400
I can't help but think about

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.700
salmonella falling into his cup right now.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.740
'Cause I bet those are not
pasteurized in shell eggs.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.250
He doesn't look like he was
fancy enough to be buying those.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.110
And salmonella,

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.070
you can go many eggs without getting it.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.399
I think the statistic
is one in 20,000 eggs

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.760
contains salmonella,

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.520
but that one time you get it,
you're gonna wish you didn't.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.530
Also, I believe that
there's a fact out there,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.330
eating raw eggs decreases
your ability to absorb biotin

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.423
which is good for hair, skin and nails.

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:49.369
- [News Anchor] Well, we deserve it.

00:00:49.369 --> 00:00:50.251
We've been getting away with murder

00:00:50.251 --> 00:00:51.595
for the last couple of weeks.

00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:53.038
Our high today could possibly be.

00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:55.274
- Why are you spilling
it on your shirt, guy?

00:00:55.274 --> 00:00:58.616
(Rocky grunting)

00:00:58.616 --> 00:00:59.449
Whoa.

00:01:01.165 --> 00:01:02.460
This is so unnecessary.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.460
Not only is he punching raw meat

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.970
that should be used for
human eating consumption,

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.840
but he's also punching ribs,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.070
hurting his knuckles

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.850
because he doesn't have boxing gloves on.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.360
As any boxer would know,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.930
an injury to your knuckles

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.797
is an injury to your
boxing career, potentially.

00:01:18.797 --> 00:01:20.740
(Rocky grunting)

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.019
- You're breaking the ribs.

00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:23.590
(doctor laughing)

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.350
- Also, he's throwing punches
in kind of like a weird form.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:27.270
I don't know what that is.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.770
He's not like throwing a straight shot.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.670
He's not throwing a hook.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.130
He's kind of like doing some kind of

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.633
in between overhand thing.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.553
Those wraps smell like death.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.380
Look, we have the same beanie
on except mine's merch.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.300
Link down below to sign up
for the new merch release,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.270
coming soon.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.860
- You lay off that pet shop dame.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.130
Women weaken legs.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.070
- The scientific accuracy
of that statement

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.270
just has never been proven to be true.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.320
Whether you look at hormone levels,

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.680
you look at performance,

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.190
it just, there is no pattern
that has emerged there.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.450
And I'll tell you why.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.600
'Cause I don't think it's women,

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.970
I don't think it's sex.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.780
I think it's the act of getting boozed up,

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.530
stressed out, staying up late.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.270
That's what weakens the legs,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.490
but it's not the women or
the sex that's causing it.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.160
I call misinformation on that one.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.610
Look at 'em on the speed bag.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:20.973
Yeah, Rocco!

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.510
(inspirational montage music)

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.620
That's actually really hard.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.600
There's an element of plyometrics there.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.610
Shoulder strengthening,
core strengthening.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.030
A lot of stuff is happening there.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.330
This is really impressive.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.010
Core training for boxing is so important

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.120
because not only are you needing
the ability to absorb hits,

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.770
but you also need the
ability to turn your body.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.870
That's how you develop strength in boxing.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.150
Can someone get this guy
a proper punching bag?

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.373
The cows need a break!

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.080
That kind of exercise on the stairs

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.320
is obviously the iconic Rocky moment.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.100
And while I think stairs
are a great exercise,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.050
I think it trains your
lower body extremely well,

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.980
your cardiovascular system extremely well,

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.740
I prefer doing like the aero bike to that

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.040
because you're getting an
upper and lower body workout

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.840
and a HIIT workout at the same time.

00:03:15.918 --> 00:03:16.751
Ooh.

00:03:20.628 --> 00:03:21.670
- Your nose is broken.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.740
- Nasal fractures are
a very common injury,

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.760
especially in boxing.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.240
40 to 50% of facial
fractures happen in the nose.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.073
But two things can happen.

00:03:29.073 --> 00:03:30.450
You could form a septal hematoma,

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.780
which is blood pooling in the area,

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.600
causing immense pressure problems

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.060
and it actually needs to be drained.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.250
And then the second
thing that could happen

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.350
is you could have a fracture
of your cribriform plate

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.070
where you actually start
leaking cerebral spinal fluid,

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.820
also known as CSF.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.416
Ooh.

00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:45.249
Ooh.

00:03:45.249 --> 00:03:46.640
Right body shots are brutal,

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:47.570
'cause not only do you have

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.650
the potential for breaking someone's ribs,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.430
which obviously is extremely painful,

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.820
hurts your ability to rotate,

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.530
hurts your ability to breathe,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.130
but also because your liver's there

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.430
and a shot to the liver,

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.210
with its unique position within the body

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.270
and its unique relationship
with the nervous system

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.000
and the circulatory system,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.747
a shot to the liver will bring you down.

00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:07.660
- I can't see nothing.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.407
Gotta open my eye.

00:04:09.407 --> 00:04:10.337
Cut me, Mick.

00:04:10.337 --> 00:04:11.170
- I don't wanna do it.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.425
- Go on, cut me.

00:04:12.425 --> 00:04:13.463
Cut me.

00:04:13.463 --> 00:04:14.713
- Okay, try it.

00:04:16.693 --> 00:04:18.433
(Rocky grunting)

00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:20.140
- This is such a terrible scene.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.530
Okay, so we no longer do this.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.930
What's happening here is he
has a hematoma over his eye,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.290
swelling, blood pooling.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.540
And essentially he's saying cut it open

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.650
so the fluid can leak out

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.400
and I can actually open my eye and see.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.410
That was done incredibly not safe.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.430
He didn't even disinfect the area first.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.500
That's gonna be a problem.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.440
Nowadays, this is not legal.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.490
Cut men are not actually cutting you.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.580
They're actually stopping
cuts from bleeding

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.300
and gauging on whether or not

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.370
the cut is dangerous to the
person's life or vital organs.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.374
- Come on, Rocky!

00:04:48.374 --> 00:04:49.660
Go on and get him.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.010
Get him, get him, get him.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.629
Come on, what's the matter with ya?

00:04:52.629 --> 00:04:53.462
Get him!

00:04:53.462 --> 00:04:56.330
- But there's better ways to do training

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.730
than torturing a poor
chicken running around.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.050
There's just exercises you could do

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.646
where you don't need to chase a chicken.

00:05:02.646 --> 00:05:04.510
- My husband and I thank you for

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.580
coming to our training quarter today.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.760
- Well, hello, my fellow
Russian immigrant.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.590
I'm glad to face you.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.060
- There have been rumors of blood doping

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.880
and widespread distribution
of anabolic steroids

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.080
in the Soviet Union.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.585
Has Drago partaken in
any such experiments?

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.418
- No.

00:05:20.418 --> 00:05:21.730
- Anabolic steroids, blood doping.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.720
It is a real thing in professional sports.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.380
Even though there are steps
put in place to prevent it,

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.330
like drug testing.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.830
Russia also had a huge scandal
with anabolic steroids.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:31.910
I highly recommend,

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.210
there's a documentary on
Netflix called Icarus.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.320
Definitely check that out,

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.430
'cause it just shows
you how dirty and nasty

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:39.670
all of these games are behind the scenes.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.420
(dramatic music)

00:05:47.188 --> 00:05:48.810
- As you can see,

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.453
Drago averages 1,850 pounds.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.146
So the result's quite obvious.

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:56.100
(crickets chirping)

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.230
- That he's strong?

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.970
What does the technology
have to do with it?

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.730
This guy didn't describe anything.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.950
It looks like he created
those arcade things

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:05.420
that you see on TikTok
videos of people failing

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:08.312
and hitting the top of it
and breaking their hands.

00:06:08.312 --> 00:06:09.145
- [Commentator] I've never seen Apollo

00:06:09.145 --> 00:06:10.332
take so much punishment.

00:06:10.332 --> 00:06:11.716
- Get the towel!

00:06:11.716 --> 00:06:13.371
- No!

00:06:13.371 --> 00:06:14.450
- Oh.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.530
Yeah, the reason the referee
has come in and step in

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:20.390
or the corner has to throw
in the towel is because

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:23.130
the fighter no longer can
make decisions for themselves.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.250
If you take too many punches to the head,

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.640
it's very easy to find
yourself in that position.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:28.590
So if you see a fighter

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.960
that's just getting hit
repeatedly, repeatedly,

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.650
not being able to throw back

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.750
not being able to show

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.770
that he's doing any kind
of movement or action,

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.290
that puts his life in jeopardy.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.440
That's where it gets
shut down and stopped.

00:06:42.608 --> 00:06:44.180
- My God!

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:47.640
- What's interesting is that
a lot of the deadly blows

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.370
and most damaging blows in boxing

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.580
come over a period of time,

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.850
multiple blows over, over, over again,

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.450
not like that one strong knockout

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.880
that actually ends up knocking you down.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.480
And there's a lot problems

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.900
when you start having
bleeding in the brain

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.000
because the skull is an
enclosed environment.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.440
There's nowhere for that blood to go.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:05.880
So if the person starts bleeding,

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.170
A, they're not getting blood flow

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.260
to the actual part of their
brain that's necessary,

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.850
but it also starts building up pressure,

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.300
putting more pressure on the brain,

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.490
essentially shutting
parts of the brain down.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.840
If your brain stem shuts down,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.280
the part that's responsible
for respiratory rate

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.120
or cardiac rate,

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.594
that shuts down, that's when you die.

00:07:21.594 --> 00:07:22.694
- If he dies, he dies.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.981
- Rocco, where are the chest compressions?

00:07:26.981 --> 00:07:28.830
(hands slapping)

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.110
You don't know why he's dying.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.630
What if he's bleeding internally

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:32.940
and needs some chest compressions?

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.328
Check his pulse, Rocco.

00:07:34.328 --> 00:07:36.995
(ominous music)

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.210
I guess that guy is roiding,

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.820
but it's not clear what that was.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.850
And earlier it was
mentioned, blood doping.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.540
Blood doping is basically

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.500
either getting transfusions of blood,

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.660
either from yourself or from someone else,

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:53.740
or they give themselves
a chemical known as EPO,

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.730
erythropoietin,

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:56.820
which is actually a chemical
made by your kidneys

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.880
that increased the production
of red blood cells,

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.840
thereby increasing your
oxygen carrying ability.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.750
- He's cut!
- Oh.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.763
- He's cut.

00:08:04.763 --> 00:08:05.596
- [Commentator] The Russian's cut!

00:08:05.596 --> 00:08:07.470
- Russian's cut?

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.241
It's kind of a weird way to say it.

00:08:09.241 --> 00:08:11.600
(bell ringing)

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:12.940
That last punch was so fake.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:13.773
It was bad.

00:08:13.773 --> 00:08:15.760
Like, he just went like this
and nothing even happened.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.055
And there was the sound effect.

00:08:18.055 --> 00:08:20.805
(crowd cheering)

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.510
- All right!

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.560
- Boxing actually has
this 10 count, right?

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.530
There's a person who
stands outside the ring

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.990
and actually starts the
count and holds the count.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.140
Also once a fighter is up,

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:35.320
it doesn't necessarily mean
they're ready to fight.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.700
If the referee deems

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.370
that the fighter is not
able to protect themselves,

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.360
like if the referee's like
move left, move right,

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:41.930
hold up your arms in front of you,

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:42.950
if you're unable to do that,

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.320
that means you're unable
to protect yourself.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.220
The fight is still over.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.020
- Rocky, you're scaring me.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.103
What's wrong?

00:08:49.043 --> 00:08:50.427
- I can't.

00:08:50.427 --> 00:08:51.510
- Can't what?

00:08:54.024 --> 00:08:57.420
- I can't stop my hands from shaking.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.250
- I mean, maybe it's a good
time to go to the hospital?

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.692
- I'm just tired.

00:09:01.692 --> 00:09:02.525
- Okay.

00:09:02.525 --> 00:09:04.420
- And I just wanna go home, okay?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.390
- At this point there
should be a ring physician

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.640
or a ringside physician

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.550
coming in, doing a neuro check,

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.130
making sure that,
neurologically, he's intact,

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.810
he's fine, he's stable.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.820
And I don't feel like
that's happening here.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.200
- Recently, The American
Medical Association

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.100
recommended that boxing be banned.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:21.933
- Yeah?

00:09:21.933 --> 00:09:23.060
- Do you agree with the doctor?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.770
- Is boxing a dangerous sport

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.680
that is unhealthy for your brain?

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.513
Yes.

00:09:27.513 --> 00:09:29.780
Is there a way to practice boxing,

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.160
practice boxing, not actually
fight, and be healthy?

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:33.993
Yes.

00:09:33.993 --> 00:09:35.890
In fact, there's a lot of
healthy benefits to boxing.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.960
When you're calculating
someone's risk in their life,

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.730
you're not just looking at one activity.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:42.200
There's a lot of variables.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.800
Those who step inside the ring

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.590
and risk getting hit in the face

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:48.330
and cause CTE to their
brain, they're taking a risk.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.840
I think it's their choice.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:51.440
I think a lot of people make that choice.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.290
- You know, absolutely.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.430
I think that doctors
should never fight, no.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.760
- Did he just say that I shouldn't fight?

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:59.190
Rocco, I'm sorry buddy, but I gotta do it!

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:02.200
- Because of the continuous
violent blows to the head,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.510
you've developed a condition
particular to boxers

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:06.840
called cavum septum pellucidum,

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:10.240
which is a hole in the membrane
separating the ventricles.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.770
The brain surface neurons in this area

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.110
have also been traumatized.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.240
- I don't even know what the
heck they're looking at here.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.360
It says physical.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.740
There's some kind of beautiful lines.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.930
There's different cuts
that we're looking at here.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.240
Maybe a functional MRI, like an early one.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.610
The reality is the condition
they're talking about

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.110
is one that has been
associated, not proven,

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:31.670
to have happened with
contact sport athletes,

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.640
fighters, football players, et cetera.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.820
It's been associated with CTE,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.530
chronic trauma encephalopathy.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:41.090
We have tied the condition
to worse mood outcomes,

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:41.990
worse scores,

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.740
but it's also something that
can happen during development

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.500
and be an incidental finding

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.980
and sort of like a normal
variant on imaging.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.430
So there's still a lot of
questions to be answered.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.900
What causes this exactly?

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.010
How does it happen?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.870
Because there's only
theories out there so far.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.360
And what are the implications
if it does happen

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.780
if you've never had it before?

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:02.890
And in fact, I know in
the future Rocky movies,

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:03.940
he goes back to fighting.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.370
So clearly this wasn't a
reason for him to retire.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.070
- I think I want to, like, do something.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.400
- Like what?

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.233
- Fight.

00:11:12.211 --> 00:11:15.650
(inspirational montage music)

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.780
- I don't know that you
need to squat 10 plates

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.347
in order to be a boxer.

00:11:19.347 --> 00:11:20.180
(doctor laughing)

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.110
And he loves his raw eggs.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.900
My man, just get some whey protein powder.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:23.923
This is ridiculous.

00:11:27.178 --> 00:11:30.000
He's literally asking to
tear his bicep by doing that.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.460
Oh my God, he's punching the cows again.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.738
Just, God.

00:11:33.738 --> 00:11:36.488
(crowd cheering)

00:11:38.334 --> 00:11:41.066
The effects got better,
but not much better.

00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:41.930
- [Commentator] And back comes Dixon

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.530
with brutal left hand shots.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.363
- Oh!

00:11:44.363 --> 00:11:45.196
- [Commentator] Dickson
hurt his hand there.

00:11:45.196 --> 00:11:48.700
- Hitting another fighter's
bone with a bad angle

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:49.800
is very problematic.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.633
Elbow,

00:11:50.633 --> 00:11:51.960
you go to hit a body shot,

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.210
the elbow hits you in
the thumb, in the wrist,

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.720
it could potentially break your hand.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.550
Hitting someone in the hip, bad angle,

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.920
can turn the wrist, sprain it, break it.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.820
Another one is on the skull.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.500
You go to punch a fighter,
they tilt their skull down.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.330
It flexes your wrist like
this, over flexes it,

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:11.050
potentially sprains,
tears, breaks bone here.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:12.384
- How's the hand?

00:12:12.384 --> 00:12:13.217
- My hand's broke.

00:12:13.217 --> 00:12:14.210
- How's the hand?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.043
My hand's broke.

00:12:15.043 --> 00:12:15.960
That's it, throw in the fight.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.360
There's no need to continue.

00:12:21.089 --> 00:12:23.071
- What did you said to the kid?

00:12:23.071 --> 00:12:25.170
It ain't about how hard you hit,

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.850
it's about how hard you can get hit

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.730
and keep moving forward.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.410
- Uh, that's not exactly true.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:34.481
Boxing is the sport of
hitting and not getting hit.

00:12:34.481 --> 00:12:37.470
Rocco is not the only boxer in the house.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.920
This doctor is a boxer, too.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.100
Click here to check that out.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.070
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.200
Click here, check it out.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.117
(electronic music)

00:12:49.249 --> 00:12:51.295
Who else do you know who
can box in office chair?

00:12:51.295 --> 00:12:52.128
Huh?

